---
const guide = '/images/webmaker-guide';
const exe = 'https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/releases/download/v0.2.0/WebMAKER.Studio_0.2.0_x64-setup.exe';
const msi = 'https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/releases/download/v0.2.0/WebMAKER.Studio_0.2.0_x64_en-US.msi';
---
<div class="tutorial-intro">
  <p>WebMAKER Studio 0.2.0 is a stable Windows release. Its guided Create Club workflow can build and publish a clean club project without asking a normal user to clone the WebMAKER source. The diagrams below are illustrations using the fictional Aurora Sport Club.</p>
  <p><a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/blob/main/docs/create-club.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Create Club guide ↗</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/releases/tag/v0.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebMAKER 0.2.0 release notes ↗</a></p>
</div>

<nav class="tutorial-paths" aria-label="Choose a tutorial path"><a href="#user-guide">For users: install & use</a><a href="#developer-guide">For contributors & developers</a></nav>

<div class="tutorial-path-heading" id="user-guide"><p class="eyebrow">For users</p><h3>Install & use WebMAKER</h3><p>Create a basketball or football club from Studio, optionally publish it to a public GitHub repository, then keep the content and design up to date without working in the WebMAKER source repository.</p></div>

<ol class="tutorial-steps">
  <li class="tutorial-step">
    <div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">01 / Install</span><h3>Install Studio and Git</h3><p><a class="inline-link" href={exe}>Download WebMAKER Studio 0.2.0 for Windows ↗</a>. The installer is unsigned, so Windows may show an Unknown publisher notice. An <a class="inline-link" href={msi}>alternative MSI package ↗</a> is also available.</p><p>Install Git for Windows with Git Credential Manager before using GitHub features. Git is optional if you only create and edit a local club. Studio does not place a personal access token in the project.</p></div>
    <figure><img src={`${guide}/02-studio.svg`} alt="Illustration of the WebMAKER Studio home screen with Create a new club, Clone from GitHub and Open existing project actions" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Choose the workflow that matches your club project. Illustration.</figcaption></figure>
  </li>
  <li class="tutorial-step">
    <div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">02 / Create Club</span><h3>Describe the first club project</h3><p>Open Studio and select <strong>Create a new club</strong>. Enter the club name, short name, basketball or football profile, Bold, Classic or Dynamic theme, first season, folder name and destination. Studio will never overwrite an existing destination folder.</p></div>
    <figure><img src={`${guide}/04-create-club.svg`} alt="Illustration of the WebMAKER Create Club form for fictional Aurora Sport Club with sport, theme, season and destination fields" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Set the club identity, sport, theme, first season and local destination. Illustration.</figcaption></figure>
  </li>
  <li class="tutorial-step">
    <div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">03 / Optional GitHub</span><h3>Connect and publish</h3><p>Select <strong>Create and publish a GitHub repository</strong> if the club should go online. Sign in through the browser window opened by Git Credential Manager, choose the GitHub user or organization, and enter the repository name. This release creates public repositories only. An organization may require additional policy approval.</p><p>Select <strong>Create club</strong>. Studio creates the local project, initializes a clean <code>main</code> branch, creates the public repository, pushes the project and enables the included GitHub Pages workflow.</p></div>
    <figure><img src={`${guide}/05-github-publish.svg`} alt="Illustration of optional GitHub publishing settings for the fictional Aurora Sport Club" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>GitHub publishing is optional and uses Git Credential Manager. Illustration.</figcaption></figure>
  </li>
  <li class="tutorial-step">
    <div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">04 / Verify Pages</span><h3>Wait for the live website</h3><p>A successful push does not mean deployment is complete. Open the repository on GitHub, wait for the Pages workflow in <strong>Actions</strong> to finish, then open and check the public site. Local creation remains useful if the optional remote step fails.</p></div>
    <figure><img src={`${guide}/03-pages.svg`} alt="Illustration showing Install Studio, Create Club, Connect GitHub and Verify Pages in sequence" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Install Studio, create the club, connect GitHub and verify Pages. Illustration.</figcaption></figure>
  </li>
  <li class="tutorial-step">
    <div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">05 / Existing project</span><h3>Already have a WebMAKER project?</h3><p>Choose <strong>Clone from GitHub</strong> when the WebMAKER repository is not yet on this computer. Choose <strong>Open existing project</strong> when the repository has already been cloned locally. Studio validates the project before opening it.</p></div>
    <figure><img src={`${guide}/06-existing-project.svg`} alt="Illustration comparing Clone from GitHub with Open existing project in WebMAKER Studio" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Clone a remote project or open one that already exists locally. Illustration.</figcaption></figure>
  </li>
  <li class="tutorial-step">
    <div class="step-copy"><span class="section-kicker">06 / Customize</span><h3>Make the club site yours</h3><p>Use Studio to update the club identity, logo, colors, sport profile, theme, teams, players, rosters, seasons, competitions, games, results and news. Publish only media you have permission to use.</p><p>For AI assistance, provide only the relevant configuration and synthetic examples. Review every diff and run the project tests before publishing. Never put credentials, private player information, personal information about minors or unlicensed media into a prompt.</p></div>
    <figure><img src={`${guide}/01-themes.svg`} alt="Illustration comparing Bold, Classic and Dynamic layouts with the same fictional Aurora Sport Club data" width="960" height="440" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>One fictional club, three site themes. Illustration.</figcaption></figure>
  </li>
</ol>

<div class="tutorial-path-heading" id="developer-guide"><p class="eyebrow">For contributors & developers</p><h3>Improve WebMAKER</h3><p>The source workflow remains available as an advanced alternative. Normal Studio users do not need these commands.</p></div>
<div class="developer-guide-grid">
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>1. Use the advanced source initializer</h4><p>Install Node.js 22 or newer and Git. The initializer creates an independent club project with fictional data and its own Pages workflow.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker.git
cd webmaker
node scripts/init-club.mjs ../my-club</code></pre></div>
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>2. Build and test locally</h4><p>Use fictional fixtures. Run site tests and builds, Studio tests and Rust tests before proposing a change. The repository README lists the current Windows build prerequisites.</p><pre><code>cd site &amp;&amp; npm ci &amp;&amp; npm test &amp;&amp; npm run build
cd ../studio &amp;&amp; npm ci &amp;&amp; npm test &amp;&amp; npm run build
cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml</code></pre></div>
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>3. Propose a focused change</h4><p>Check existing Issues, fork the <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebMAKER repository ↗</a>, create a focused branch and open a pull request. Keep real club media, credentials and private player data out of commits. WebMAKER is Apache-2.0 and retains its NOTICE attribution.</p></div>
  <div class="developer-guide-card"><h4>4. Preserve shared data</h4><p>Keep stable IDs and TagMAKER-compatible roster paths. Review changes against the <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/playmaker-schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">shared PlayMAKER schema ↗</a>, and provide nondestructive migrations when a stored format changes.</p></div>
</div>
